# Ansible Infrastructure Lab

A hands-on Ansible project for automating the configuration and management of multiple Linux servers.

This project is designed as a practical DevOps lab to review and reinforce Ansible fundamentals through a realistic infrastructure automation scenario.

The project currently covers server connectivity, inventory management, baseline configuration, variables, facts, user management, Nginx deployment, Jinja2 templates, handlers, service management, and HTTP verification.

---

## Project Scenario

A DevOps engineer is responsible for preparing and maintaining multiple Linux servers that will be used as web servers.

Instead of connecting to each server manually over SSH and configuring them one by one, Ansible is used to define and enforce a consistent desired state across all managed nodes.

The current lab consists of:

* 1 Ansible Control Node
* 2 Ubuntu Managed Nodes
* SSH key-based authentication
* A dedicated `ansible` automation user
* Centralized inventory management
* Automated baseline configuration
* Centralized variables
* Ansible Facts and conditions
* Automated Linux user management
* Automated Nginx installation and configuration
* Jinja2-based configuration and web page deployment
* Handler-based Nginx reload
* HTTP service verification

