## Ansible Configuration

The project contains a local `ansible.cfg` file.

Example:

```ini
[defaults]
inventory = inventory/hosts.ini
host_key_checking = True
interpreter_python = auto_silent
```

### Configuration Explanation

`inventory` defines the default inventory file:

```ini
inventory = inventory/hosts.ini
```

This allows commands such as:

```bash
ansible all -m ping
```

instead of:

```bash
ansible all -i inventory/hosts.ini -m ping
```

`host_key_checking` keeps SSH host identity verification enabled:

```ini
host_key_checking = True
```

`interpreter_python` allows Ansible to automatically discover the Python interpreter on Managed Nodes:

```ini
interpreter_python = auto_silent
```

---

## Inventory

The current inventory contains a single host group named `webservers`.

```ini
[webservers]
web01 ansible_host=192.168.1.20
web02 ansible_host=192.168.1.30

[webservers:vars]
ansible_user=ansible
ansible_ssh_private_key_file=~/.ssh/id_ed25519
```

The logical inventory hostnames are:

```text
web01
web02
```

while the actual SSH destinations are:

```text
192.168.1.20
192.168.1.30
```

The inventory structure can be inspected using:

```bash
ansible-inventory --graph
```

