## Connectivity Verification

Ansible connectivity is tested using:

```bash
ansible all -m ping
```

Expected result:

```text
web01 | SUCCESS => {
    "changed": false,
    "ping": "pong"
}

web02 | SUCCESS => {
    "changed": false,
    "ping": "pong"
}
```

Ansible Ping is not an ICMP ping.

It verifies that Ansible can:

* Locate the target host
* Establish an SSH connection
* Authenticate successfully
* Execute an Ansible module
* Use the Python interpreter on the Managed Node

