## Ansible Facts

Ansible automatically gathers system information during:

```text
TASK [Gathering Facts]
```

Facts used in this project include:

```text
ansible_distribution
ansible_distribution_version
ansible_architecture
ansible_os_family
ansible_hostname
ansible_default_ipv4
```

Facts can be inspected manually using:

```bash
ansible web01 -m setup
```

Filtered example:

```bash
ansible web01 -m setup -a "filter=ansible_distribution*"
```

---

## Conditional Execution

The project uses Facts to avoid executing distribution-specific tasks on unsupported systems.

Example:

```yaml
when: ansible_os_family == "Debian"
```

This allows APT tasks to execute on systems such as:

```text
Ubuntu
Debian
```

while being skipped on systems from other OS families.

---

## User Management

The playbook:

```text
playbooks/users.yml
```

manages a DevOps user.

The username is defined using:

```yaml
devops_user: devops
```

The playbook ensures that:

* The `devops` user exists
* `/bin/bash` is used as the login shell
* A home directory exists
* The user belongs to the `sudo` group
* Existing supplementary groups are preserved
* A secure `.ssh` directory exists

The `.ssh` directory uses:

```text
Owner: devops
Group: devops
Permission: 0700
```

User configuration can be verified using:

```bash
ansible webservers -m command -a "id devops"
```

